0,Telefol language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telefol_language,"Language family. Trans–New Guinea.Telefol has dyadic kinship terms (terms referring to the relationship two or more people have to each other), which are uncommon in the world's languages and not prevalent in Papua New Guinea.",Telefol,Trans-New Guinea
1,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Telefol,Trans-New Guinea
