6,Bougainville Traditional Bamboo Band And Telefomin ... - YouTubeTelefol language — GrokipediaMusic of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2d88cQplYO0,"Nov 10, 2020 · The next video is the traditional singing and dancing by the Telefol tribesmen in Telefomin, Papua New Guinea, who occasionally dress like this to sing and dance to show their rich cultural... The Telefol language is primarily spoken in the Telefomin District of Sandaun Province, Papua New Guinea, with the main concentration in a large central area surrounding the administrative center of Telefomin in the mountainous interior. The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Telefol,Trans-New Guinea
